st don't feel strong  it's unbelievably easy to run away from  a fight and parkour  somewhere different games began to feel  like hide and seek missions  which sucked the fun out of it for me  the game is receiving regular updates so  hopefully the weapons will feel more  balanced soon and less like water  pistols  and a little bit more deadly hyperscape  released yesterday if you're watching  the day i release this video  if you've tried it please let me know  your thoughts right now i had hoped to  talk to you about rogue company another  free-to-play game which was scheduled to  be released  right now but sadly that has been held  off for the time being and replaced with  an early adopter pack  which costs money it's a great game by  the way but let's talk about it  once it goes free to play the next game  is  perezo island probably the worst name of  a video game ever  right try this then have you heard of  animal crossing  well here is an attempt to recreate that  formula on ps4  you'll be set up on an island which has  a real time day night cycle  so if it's midnight in real life it's  midnight in the game too  the island will fill up with other  animals to create a village and your job  is to live alongside them  and craft items to upgrade your home and  theirs too  what genre would this be then a life  simulator i guess  we'll be planting and harvesting fruit  we'll be going fishing and just  generally  chilling out with your islanders i think  the main reason i'm including this game  on the list this time around is because  any money that's spent in the game will  go to real world  charities which may make me forgive how  clunky the game feels at present  ultimately if you don't have a nintendo  switch or you can't afford animal  crossing  try pareso island or not it's your life  next we have fantasy strike a street  fighter inspired one-on-one fighting  game  there's a ton of characters to choose  from and the game is super easy to play  but dedication is 